  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1177",
      "html": "<p>Scientific name: Aguarunichthys tocantinsensis Zuanon, Rapp Py-Daniel &amp; Jégu, 1993.</p><p>Common name: Tocantins Pimelodus.</p><p>Size: 317 mm (12.5 in) SL.</p><p>IUCN Red List: Endangered (last assessed 2018).</p><p>Etymology: Aguarun = a Peruvian Indian tribe that lives in Ecuador, and \"ichthys\" = Greek for fish. Named for the Rio Tocantins in Brazil.</p><p>Identification: Aguarunichthys tocantinsensis has a deeper body, larger eye, more gill rakers and more spots on the body than A. torosus.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1177",
      "html": "<p>South America: Tocantins River basin. Type locality: rapids above Marabá, Rio Tocantins drainage, Pará State, Brazil.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1177",
      "html": "<p>Collected in areas with strong currents and rocky bottom.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1177",
      "html": "<p>Will take dry food pellets, earthworms or fish fillet. Earthworms are perhaps the best staple.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1177",
      "html": "<p>A predator that will eat anything small enough. A loner, it shows considerable intra-species aggression around a large territory.</p><p>Tankmates must be large enough not to be considered edible. Competition for food is not an issue, as this species is a capable hunter.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1177",
      "html": "<p>Unreported in the aquarium.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "references",
      "source": "planetcatfish",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.planetcatfish.com/common/species.php?species_id=1177",
      "html": "<p>Ichthyological Exploration of Freshwaters v. 4 (no. 3), pp 252, Figs. 2a, 4.</p>"
    }
